{
  "title": "Can, want and go: possum, volo, eo",
  "note": "Possum, posse (can, be able) is pot- + sum: possum, potes, potest, possumus, potestis, possunt, with pot- before e and pos- before s. Volo, velle (want), nolo, nolle (not want), malo, malle (prefer) and eo, ire (go) are irregular too. They take an infinitive: Possum legere, I can read. Noli plus an infinitive means don't.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Allen and Greenough, Irregular Verbs: Compounds of sum",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/irregular-verbs-compounds-sum"
  },
